# Codex–Cursor collaboration

Before changing the repository, read and follow `docs/AI-COLLABORATION.md`.

- Check `.ai-work/claims/` and `git status --short` first.
- Create your own ignored claim from `.ai-work/CLAIM_TEMPLATE.md` before editing.
- Claim exact files. Treat directory claims and shared infrastructure files as exclusive.
- Do not touch any path covered by another active claim. If scopes overlap, choose a different task slice or ask the user to coordinate.
- Preserve every change you did not create. Never revert, delete, rename, format, stage, or commit another owner's work.
- Stage explicit owned paths only; never use broad Git staging or cleanup commands.
- Do not run repository-wide write commands while another claim is active.
- Remove only your own claim after validation, commit/handoff, and a final status check.
